{"text": " You wake up in 1928 on a crowded American beach. Everyone is lying in the sun on purpose. Once a tan meant you labored in the fields, now it means you can afford a day off. Did you know that the famous story that Coco Chanel started the Sun tan craze is probably a myth. A historian traced it to an unsigned magazine article from 1971. The real reason was work. As jobs moved into factories and offices, a tan became the badge of leisure. Then in 1954 at Bell's Laboratories, three scientists build a silicon cell that turns about 6% of sunlight into electricity. Four years later, a tiny satellite called Vanguard 1 runs a radio on sunlight. It is still circling the Earth today. We had learned to live on sunlight. Now we would fly straight into it.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 3.22, "text": " You wake up in 1928 on a crowded American beach.", "tokens": [50364, 509, 6634, 493, 294, 1294, 11205, 322, 257, 21634, 2665, 7534, 13, 50556], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12885706655440793, "compression_ratio": 1.5314685314685315, "no_speech_prob": 0.005467352457344532, "words": [{"word": " You", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.12, "probability": 0.5208783149719238}, {"word": " wake", "start": 0.12, "end": 0.28, "probability": 0.9704824686050415}, {"word": " up", "start": 0.28, "end": 0.48, "probability": 0.9989987015724182}, {"word": " in", "start": 0.48, "end": 0.58, "probability": 0.977495551109314}, {"word": " 1928", "start": 0.58, "end": 1.38, "probability": 0.9905939698219299}, {"word": " on", "start": 1.38, "end": 2.0, "probability": 0.8566120266914368}, {"word": " a", "start": 2.0, "end": 2.1, "probability": 0.9905824661254883}, {"word": " crowded", "start": 2.1, "end": 2.4, "probability": 0.9619995355606079}, {"word": " American", "start": 2.4, "end": 2.8, "probability": 0.9935556054115295}, {"word": " beach.", "start": 2.8, "end": 3.22, "probability": 0.956196665763855}]}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 3.86, "end": 5.84, "text": " Eve